---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Editorial Policy - Finsiva" description="Finsiva editorial policy and content guidelines for our tax calculators and guides.">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-8 dark:text-on-primary">Editorial Policy</h1>
        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-HJckKnwCXxQ?w=1200&q=80" alt="Editorial review and fact-checking" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />
        
        <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted">
          <p>Finsiva is committed to providing accurate, reliable, and up-to-date tax information. Our editorial policy ensures that all content meets strict quality and accuracy standards. Every article, calculator description, and guide is produced through a structured process designed to minimize errors and maximize clarity for a global audience.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Source Verification</h2>
          <p>All tax information is sourced directly from official government resources, including tax authority publications, legislation, statutory instruments, and official guidance. We maintain a record of primary sources for every tax rate, threshold, and rule we publish. Wherever possible, we include direct links to government portals, revenue circulars, or legal databases so readers can verify our claims independently.</p>
          <p>We do not rely on news articles, blog posts, or secondary summaries for rule definitions. If a rule is subject to interpretation, we consult official commentary or seek clarification from the relevant tax authority before publishing. Sources are reviewed at least quarterly to ensure they remain accessible and accurate.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Content Accuracy</h2>
          <p>All tax information is thoroughly researched and reviewed against official government sources, including tax authority publications, legislation, and official guidance. We strive to present information that is current at the time of publication. Our research team downloads the latest tax tables, budget announcements, and regulatory updates directly from government websites to ensure we are working from authoritative materials.</p>
          <p>Before any calculator goes live, our research team downloads the latest official tax tables, legislation, and guidance documents from government portals. We do not rely on secondary summaries or news articles for rule definitions. Every bracket, threshold, and deduction is traced to a primary source.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Writer Qualifications</h2>
          <p>Finsiva contributors hold professional qualifications in accounting, taxation, law, or finance. Many are certified public accountants, chartered tax advisers, or licensed tax practitioners with years of experience in both public practice and private industry. Before writing for Finsiva, contributors must demonstrate subject-matter expertise through credentials, portfolio, or reference checks.</p>
          <p>We maintain an internal directory of contributor qualifications and areas of specialization. When an article covers a complex topic such as transfer pricing, indirect tax, or cross-border payroll, it is assigned to a writer with documented experience in that specific field. This ensures that nuanced subjects receive treatment appropriate to their complexity.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Professional Review</h2>
          <p>Content is reviewed by qualified tax professionals and subject matter experts to ensure technical accuracy and clarity. Complex topics are simplified without sacrificing precision. Each article undergoes at least two review stages: one by the assigned writer and one by an independent reviewer with relevant credentials.</p>
          <p>Draft content and calculator logic undergo a mandatory peer review by a second qualified tax professional. Only after both reviewers sign off do we publish. This double-check process is our primary defense against errors that could mislead users.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Corrections Policy</h2>
          <p>Tax laws and rates change frequently. We regularly update our content to reflect the latest changes and promptly correct any errors identified by users or reviewers. If we discover an inaccuracy after publication, we will update the content as soon as possible and, where appropriate, publish a correction note explaining what changed and why.</p>
          <p>Corrections are reviewed by our editorial team within 48 hours, and verified changes are published with a transparent correction note so readers can track updates. Serious errors that could lead to financial loss or regulatory non-compliance are prioritized for immediate correction.</p>
          <p>We maintain a public changelog for major guides and calculator updates. This log includes the date of change, a summary of what was corrected, and the source that prompted the update. Readers can use this log to understand the evolution of our content and assess its reliability over time.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Updates and Corrections</h2>
          <p>Tax laws and rates change frequently. We regularly update our content to reflect the latest changes and promptly correct any errors identified by users or reviewers.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Transparency</h2>
          <p>We are transparent about the limitations of our content. When a topic is outside our area of expertise, we say so clearly. When a rule is pending or subject to litigation, we note the uncertainty and encourage users to seek professional advice. We never overstate the accuracy or completeness of our guides.</p>
          <p>Every page includes a disclaimer reminding readers that our content is for informational purposes only and does not constitute professional tax advice. We link to our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy from every page footer to ensure these documents are always accessible.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Fact-Checking Process</h2>
          <p>Before publication, every statistic, tax rate, and rule is cross-referenced against at least one official government source. Drafts are reviewed by at least one tax professional, and any conflicting information is flagged for resolution before going live.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Source Attribution</h2>
          <p>Wherever possible, we link directly to official tax authority guidance, legislation, and government publications. This allows readers to verify claims independently and access the full legal text if needed.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Reader Corrections</h2>
          <p>We encourage users to report inaccuracies. Corrections are reviewed by our editorial team within 48 hours, and verified changes are published with a transparent correction note so readers can track updates.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>All information provided on Finsiva is for general informational purposes only and does not constitute professional tax advice. Users should consult qualified tax professionals for advice specific to their circumstances.</p>
          
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Related Pages</h2>
          <p>For more information, see our <a href="/privacy" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="/terms" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/contact" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Contact</a> page, or explore our <a href="/countries" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">country guides</a> and <a href="/blogs" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">blog</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
